      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Brahmo Samaj was established in 1828 under the leadership of Raja Rammohan Roy to promote monotheism and oppose social evils.",
        "Arya Samaj, founded in 1875 by Swami Dayanand Saraswati, emphasized Vedic authority and social reform.",
        "Ramakrishna Mission was established in 1897 by Swami Vivekananda to focus on humanitarian relief and spiritual unity.",
        "The Young Bengal Movement and Prarthana Samaj were key early developments in Bengal and Western India.",
        "Muslim reform movements like the Aligarh Movement aimed at modern scientific education and social awakening."
